Product Requirements Document (PRD)

Project Name: Safe Blog

Concept: A 100% incognito messaging application cloaked as a premium, minimalist journaling and blogging app.
Platform: Android & iOS (Flutter)
Backend: Node.js (Express) deployed on Vercel (Serverless)
Database: MongoDB
Real-Time Architecture: Server-Sent Events (SSE) & Background Polling (100% Custom, No Firebase/Pusher)

1. Executive Summary

The primary objective of Safe Blog is to provide a highly secure, private messaging environment that completely masks its true identity. When opened, it functions as a beautifully designed personal journaling platform. However, a hidden universal lock screen routes users to a fully functional, end-to-end encrypted, Telegram-style private chat interface upon entering a specific "Secret PIN."

2. Core Mechanics (The Stealth Engine)

Dual-PIN Lock Screen (The Gatekeeper):

App opens to a standard PIN pad.

Entering Blog PIN (e.g., 1234) opens the Decoy Safe Blog.

Entering Safe PIN (e.g., 9999) plays a 1.5s fake "Syncing Entries" animation, then routes to Private Chat.

Ghost Notifications (Vercel-Friendly):

Handled via Flutter workmanager (background API polling) to fetch new messages.

Incoming private messages trigger local push notifications disguised as generic journaling prompts (e.g., "Daily Prompt: What are you grateful for today?").

Tapping the notification requires PIN entry. Blog PIN opens a dummy blog; Safe PIN opens the chat.

User Discovery: Users search for other Safe Blog users via exact Username or Email within the Secret Interface.

Panic Switch (Quick Escape): A physical gesture (e.g., double-tapping the app bar) instantly kills the chat UI and flips back to the Decoy Blog.

3. Architecture & Tech Stack

Frontend (Flutter)

UI Framework: Material 3 / Cupertino.

State Management: Riverpod or Bloc.

Local Storage: flutter_secure_storage for PINs, JWT, and encrypted chat caching.

Background Tasks: workmanager for background message polling.

Backend (Node.js on Vercel)

Framework: Express.js optimized for Vercel Serverless Functions.

Real-time: Server-Sent Events (SSE) for active chat streaming, fallback to short-polling.

Auth: Custom JWT via google-auth-library (Google OAuth 2.0).

Database (MongoDB)

Strict collection isolation between decoy data and secret data.

4. UI/UX Specifications (Based on 14 Ref Screenshots)

4.1 Interface A: The Decoy App (Safe Blog Mode)

Vibe: Aesthetic, calming, premium.

Typography: Serif (Titles) & Sans-serif (Body).

Colors: Dark Theme (#121212), Light Theme (Off-white/Cream). Accent: Orange/Gold.

Layout: Bottom navigation (Today, Explore, Calendar, Profile), center (+) FAB, mood tags.

4.2 Interface B: The Secret App (Private Chat Mode)

Vibe: Utilitarian, familiar (Telegram architecture).

Colors: Standard dark blue-grey (Dark) / clean white (Light) with muted outgoing bubbles.

Layout: Top app bar with folders, circular avatars, standard messaging bubbles, read receipts.

5. MongoDB Database Schema Models

1. Users

_id, googleId (String), email (String), username (String), blogPinHash (String), safePinHash (String)

2. DecoyBlogs

_id, userId (Ref: Users), title (String), content (String), mood (String), createdAt (Date)

3. PrivateChats

_id, participants (Array of Refs: Users), lastMessageAt (Date)

4. Messages

_id, chatId (Ref: PrivateChats), senderId (Ref: Users), text (String), isRead (Boolean), timestamp (Date)